{{also|bohemian}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|Bohemia|ian}}

In sense of [[Romani]] and by association, marginalized artists, from {{uder|en|fr|bohémien||person from [[Bohemia]], [[Romani]]}}, from {{m|fr|Bohême||[[Bohemia]]}}. Regarding the sense evolution, compare {{m|en|gypsy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/boʊˈhimi.ən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A native or resident of [[Bohemia]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
# {{lb|en|now|rare}} A [[Gypsy]], a [[Romani]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
# {{alt case|en|bohemian}}; someone known for flouting social conventions, especially someone involved in the arts. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}

